	<h2>The Provenance Standard: Total Evidentiary Transparency</h2>
	<p>
		To protect readers, ensure unassailable credibility, and establish institutional accountability, every story in the ErrorLedger repository belongs to one of four strict <strong>Provenance Tiers</strong>, rendered explicitly at the top of each case file:
	</p>

	<ul>
		<li>
			<strong>Tier 1 — Documented Incident (Real Public Events):</strong>
			<br/>
			Events backed by verifiable public records (court filings, official disclosures, SEC filings, primary engineering post-mortems, corroborated investigative journalism). 
			<em>Strict Mandate: Absolute zero invention. All names, figures, timelines, and technical triggers are strictly cited from primary evidence records.</em>
		</li>
		<li>
			<strong>Tier 2 — Direct Submission (First-Person Account):</strong>
			<br/>
			Genuine accounts submitted by participants or scrubbed from verified public engineering forums. Identifying names, companies, and credentials are obfuscated to protect privacy, but core sequence dynamics are preserved.
		</li>
		<li>
			<strong>Tier 3 — Editorial Reconstruction:</strong>
			<br/>
			Narrative synthesis based on multiple documented accounts. Structural facts, mistakes, and outcomes are rigorously verified; non-essential connective dialogue is reconstructed for narrative clarity.
		</li>
		<li>
			<strong>Tier 4 — The Fiction Ledger:</strong>
			<br/>
			Speculative drama exploring psychological and systemic failure modes in a fictional scenario. Explicitly badged and isolated.
		</li>
	</ul>

	<h2>The Claim Firewall: Anti-Invention Rules</h2>
	<p>
		The ErrorLedger newsroom enforces three core rules to prevent speculative distortion:
	</p>
	<ol>
		<li><strong>No Hallucinated Psychology:</strong> We never assert an actor's private thoughts, secret emotions, or hidden motives as established fact unless supported by primary testimony, court depositions, or personal journals.</li>
		<li><strong>Authentic Community Consensus:</strong> Reader Verdict tallies reflect authentic reader interaction. We never manufacture fake social proof.</li>
		<li><strong>The Anti-AI-Slop Mandate:</strong> We ban generic AI cliches (*"delve"*, *"in conclusion"*, *"testament to"*), repetitive sentence rhythms, and unearned profundity. Every sentence must reveal character, advance conflict, or expose systemic tension.</li>
	</ol>

	<h2>The 10-Phase Editorial Lifecycle</h2>
	<p>
		Every investigation is compiled through a 10-phase forensic lifecycle:
	</p>
	<ol>
		<li><strong>Source Intelligence:</strong> Sourcing primary technical disclosures, court filings, and witness testimonies.</li>
		<li><strong>Fact System & Timeline:</strong> Building an absolute chronological claim graph with contradiction resolution.</li>
		<li><strong>Human Psychology & Failure Mechanism:</strong> Diagnosing the rationalization loop and environmental incentives that made the mistake possible.</li>
		<li><strong>Scene Architecture:</strong> Designing narrative tension, turning points, and dramatic pacing.</li>
		<li><strong>Drafting & The Archivist's Voice:</strong> Writing with narrative momentum, wit, and emotional honesty.</li>
		<li><strong>Adversarial QA & Fact Prosecution:</strong> Auditing drafts for factual drift, overstatements, or unverified claims.</li>
		<li><strong>Human Quality Audit:</strong> Eliminating filler, pacing bottlenecks, and artificial padding.</li>
		<li><strong>Packaging:</strong> Crafting accurate, high-curiosity titles and platform hooks.</li>
		<li><strong>SEO & Schema Mapping:</strong> Semantic entity structuring and verified NewsArticle metadata.</li>
		<li><strong>Publishing Gate:</strong> Multi-gate validation and static compilation.</li>
	</ol>

	<h2>Corrections & Verification</h2>
	<p>
		If you are a participant in a documented incident or have supplementary primary documentation, we invite review via our <a href="/contact">Editorial Inquiries channel</a>. All verified factual corrections are appended transparently to the incident log.
	</p>
